  "step1_summary": "- Chief complaint: Pain on urination (dysuria).\n- Symptoms: Dysuria for 6 days; lower central abdominal (suprapubic) pain, intermittent, severity ~7/10; malodorous urine; visible blood in urine described as spots (hematuria); able to pass urine; no fever or feeling feverish; no loin/flank pain; no vaginal discharge; no change in appetite or bowel habit; first episode.\n- Past medical history: Irritable bowel syndrome (IBS) only; no prior UTIs reported.\n- Medications / Allergies: Mebeverine 200 mg three times daily; allergy to clindamycin.\n- Family / Social history: Lives with friends; works as a support worker; drinks occasionally (≈1 glass wine/week); non-smoker; no family medical problems reported.\n- Vital signs / exam findings: None documented in transcript (physician asked patient to check temperature at home; no temperature recorded).\n- Labs / Imaging: None performed or documented during this visit.",
